    <!-- Science-of-closing-your-eyes quotes shown on Home. The two arrays are parallel. -->
    <string-array name="afk_eye_fact_texts">
        <item>Close your eyes and the brain slips into alpha rhythm — the 8–12 Hz wave of calm, wakeful rest.</item>
        <item>Nearly a third of your cortex is devoted to vision. Shut your eyes and you hand that capacity back.</item>
        <item>Eyes closed, the default mode network takes over — where the mind wanders, reflects, and consolidates.</item>
        <item>A brief eyes-closed pause lowers cortical arousal, slows the breath, and settles the heart rate.</item>
        <item>Just 60 seconds with eyes shut measurably reduces visual fatigue and mental load.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="afk_eye_fact_sources">
        <item>Berger · first human EEG, 1929</item>
        <item>visual neuroscience</item>
        <item>Raichle · default mode network</item>
